{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a 1 GiB file-backed LUKS2 encrypted XFS volume mounted at /srv/secure. It unlocks and mounts automatically through systemd using /etc/crypttab and /etc/fstab. The RHEL 10.0 release and kernel remain unchanged, SELinux remains enforcing, SSH remains available, and no failed units remain. Reboot persistence was verified with a changed boot identity and preserved data checksum.","actions_performed":["Installed the signed RHEL cryptsetup 2.8.1 package.","Generated a node-local root-only unlock key.","Created the LUKS2 encrypted backing volume and XFS filesystem.","Configured native systemd boot-time unlocking and mounting.","Verified incorrect-key rejection and absence of plaintext data in the encrypted backing file.","Rebooted node1 safely and verified automatic recovery, data integrity, write access, administrative access, and cleanup.","Retained restricted rollback copies under /root/secure-volume-rollback."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure","command_ids":["cmd-b7568100806a43c4","cmd-19bd187506ba4dcc","cmd-c49c3c67040449e0"],"summary":"Shows the active AES-XTS LUKS2 mapping, XFS filesystem mounted at /srv/secure, restricted permissions, incorrect-key rejection, and absence of the plaintext marker from the backing file."},{"requirement":"Automatic unlock and mount at boot","command_ids":["cmd-96ae2d3c6b894289","cmd-9debd02a19394169","cmd-2a5f74ef8bed4198"],"summary":"Shows crypttab/fstab integration, a successful systemd-managed unlock/remount cycle, and active cryptsetup and mount units sourced from those files after reboot."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel preserved","command_ids":["cmd-ea2ef49a11ec4249","cmd-2a5f74ef8bed4198"],"summary":"Before and after evidence shows RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 unchanged."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-e8a766093780441b","cmd-5d9a4233543f4785","cmd-a52e21d981874fa9","cmd-2a5f74